      "lineNbr": 6184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T12:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1.Yes they are not hard but the CL is already too big. Done in aosp/2742874 See if it works for you.\n\n2. The plan is to listen to ACTION_RESTRICT_BACKGROUND_CHANGED.\nAs discussed offline this is racy.\nBut unlikely we have a better idea for short-term.\nAnd the impact for data stall detection is not significant.\nGiven that the callpath (NPMS -\u003e NMS -\u003e netd) are all platform code, we don\u0027t have a hook point to know the status.\nIn long term, for new devices, at least we can write that into a bpf map while writing to netd.\nOr we can make bw_data_saver hook to a bpf program that checks the map in order to control data saver status. + @maze@google.com to input whether we have on-going plan related to data saver or which way is more preferred.",
      "parentUuid": "9b179b5e_ffc68b13",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6183,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 6184,
        "endChar": 32
